1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was an impressive looking man with a large, powerful physique.  He was found guilty of manslaughter in 1306, went abroad and became a King’s Guard at the Court of King Hakon of Norway.  The King made him his tax
2 CONC  collector up north in Finmark.  He was in battle with King Hakon against the Swedes, was captured but later released after a ransom had been paid.  He then returned, and in 1313 he married Þurid, daughter of Ogmund Þhordarsson of
2 CONC  Bæ.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sources  1.[S335] Islenzkar æviskrár frá landnámstímum til ársloka 1940 (1948-1976), Páll Eggert Ólason, Jón Guðnason, and Ólafur Þ. Kristjánsson, (6 volumes. Reykjavík : Hid Íslenzka Bókmenntafélags, 1948-1952, 1976), FHL book 94
2 CONC 9.12 D3p., Vol 2, p.85.
