1 NOTE {geni:about_me} of Sudavik (his estate was in West Sudavik). He took part in the Floa Battle as an ally of Þord Kakala on June 25, 1244.  It was the only naval battle fought near Iceland.  Opposed were Þord kakala Sighvatsson, nep
2 CONC hew of Snorra Sturlsson, and Kolbein the Younger Arnorsson.  They were fighting for power in the land.  Þord had twelve ships and Kolbein had twenty.  They fought in the Huna Flow and between seventy and eighty men were killed.
