1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NB! Little is known for sure about Grundar-Helga's ancestry, and everything that has been recorded about her ancestry is probably pure guesswork.
2 CONT
2 CONT of Vatnsfjord.  Called Grundar-Helga, as she was instrumental in precipitating the Battle of Grund in 1361 when Governor-General Smithur was killed.  Her husband Einar of Vatnsfjord was a very rich man.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://is.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bj%C3%B6rn_Einarsson_J%C3%B3rsalafari
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Helga had the title of Grundar Helga, well known for the Grundar Battle of July 8, 1362.  She was considered the third highest-ranking woman in Iceland in the Middle Ages.   Se was responsible for the Grundar Battle where 14 men l
2 CONC ost their lives.  
