1 OCCU Travels to Norway, Denmark and Constantinople, takes over Snorri the Priest´s estate at Saelingsdale Tongue
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Handsome Varangian" - Varangian Bolli 'Prúði' or Bolli Bollason,"the Elegant" (prúðr meant probably handsome) - The Laxdœla Saga, informs that the Icelandic Bolli Bollason, born c. 1000, was the first known Ice
2 CONC lander or Norwegian (West Norse/Viking) in the Varangian Guard. Bolli was ROLLO's great-great-great-grandson. - The Saga says: “...Wherever the group (he and his men) stopped for the night, the women could do nothing but gaze at B
2 CONC olli and the finery which he and his companions bore”. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bolli Bollason (also Bolli Bollison) was a key historical character in the Medieval Icelandic Laxdæla saga, born around 1000.[1] He grew up in Orlygsstadir, at Helgafell on the Snæfellsnes Peninsula in Iceland. He divided his time
2 CONC  between Helgafell and Tunga, the home of Snorri the Goði.[Note 1] He was held in the highest regard among the contemporary Scandinavian rulers, and also in the Byzantine Empire, where he became the first known West Norseman in th
2 CONC e Varangian Guard.[Note 2] It is believed that he had reached the rank of manglabites in the Byzantine army,[2] and on his return to Iceland, his finery and recognition earned him the name "Bolli the Elegant".[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT His importance in the literary context of the saga is his prominence as the son of Bolli Þorleiksson and Guðrún Ósvífursdóttir, the two central characters of the work. He is mentioned at the end of the Sneglu-Hall þáttur (The Tale
2 CONC  of Sarcastic Halli), and is also the subject of his own tale, the Bollaþáttur, which was later appended to the end of the manuscripts in the early 14th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.pinterest.com/pin/521291725594341441/
