1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Alfdis fra Barrø  (Álfdís Konálsdóttir)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bondekone på Vest Island'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 875 Hun var født på Barra (Barroy), Hebridene. Datter av Konall Steinmodsson, moren er ukjent 
2 CONT * ca 920 Gift med Olaf Fellan. De hadde barna Thord Gellir, Ingjald, Grane, Tora, Helga, Thorunn og Thordis 
2 CONT * Hun er omtalt i "Castle in the Sea" om klanen mac Neil av Irland  den sier at Àlfdis av Barra var den første kvinnen fra den lille øya Barra i Hebridene som ble kjent i verdenshistorien da hun giftet seg med Olaf.Fellan 
2 CONT
2 CONT Álfdís Konálsdóttir  Tilnavn / fordanskning: Alfdis fra Barrø Lokalitet: Vestl. Island. Relationer: Gift med Olaf Feilan  Kilder: Landnamabogen: S109, 334 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landnamabogen
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Barra is a small island, one of the outermost of the Hebrides, closest to Ireland.  The late Robert Lister MacNeil, 45th Chieftan of the MacNeils of Barra, in his history of the clan called "Castle in the Sea" states that Àlfdis o
2 CONC f Barra was the first woman of Barra ever to be known in world history when she married Olaf.
2 CONT
2 CONT The MacNeil further states that their (Olaf & Àlfdis') descendants are members of this clan and that it is the biggest and oldest of the clans.  The Clan descends from Niall (Neil) of the Nine Hostages, who became High King of Ire
2 CONC land in 379. Niall is the "eponym" or "name man" of Clan MacNeil, he is reckoned as the first Chief of the Clan.  
2 CONT
2 CONT It is said that Niall's son Eoghan was baptized by St. Patrick. Eogan's grandson Muirceartach is said to have given the Stone of Destiny (Stone of Scone) to his grand-uncle Fergus, King of Dalriada, Scotland.  The seat is Kisimul 
2 CONC Castle, first occupied in 1030 AD.
