1 NOTE Som en reaksjon på økende skatter og stadig forverrede levekår, gjorde Petur Delyan i 1040 opprør mot bysantinerveldet. Med sin hær inntok han Skopje og dominerte snart Trakia, Epirus og Makedonia. I 1041 ble Delyan imidlertid for
2 CONC rådt av sine allierte, blindet og tatt til fange av bysantinske tropper under kommando av blant andre Harald Hardråde. 
2 CONT Harald 3 Hardråde (1015-66) kjempet som 15-åring i slaget på Stiklestad i 1030 der hans halvbror Olav den Hellige ble drept. Etter slaget flyktet Harald gjennom Gardariket (Russland) til Konstantinopel, der han tok tjeneste hos de
2 CONC n bysantinske keiser i 1034. I flere år kjempet han for keiseren, spesielt i Bulgaria og på Sicilia. På vei hjem gjennom Gardariket giftet han seg med Ellisiv, datter av storfyrst Jaroslav i Kiev. I 1045 kom han tilbake til Norge 
2 CONC og ble anerkjent som konge sammen med Olav's sønn Magnus den Gode. Da Magnus døde i 1047, hersket Harald alene. 
2 CONT Harald 3 Hardråde falt i slaget ved Stamford Brigde i England 25. september 1066. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT half-brother of Olaf Haraldson, joined him in the fateful Battle of Stikledstad aged 15. Fleeing to Sweden and from there to Russia he served first the Grand Duke Jaroslaw of Kiev before he continued service for the Emperor in Byz
2 CONC anz (Constantinopolis) in the Warägergard. Bishop Adam of Bremen (Germany) called him "Blitzstrahl des Nordens" (flashlight of the North).  In 1045 Harald returned to Norway to gain the throne for himself. Harthacnut King of Engla
2 CONC nd had given the Danish possessions to Magnus. In 1042 these possessions were claimed by Sven, son of Knut's sister and Harald Sigurdarson took Svens side in the subsequent quarrel thus succeeding to the throne after Magnus' death
2 CONC . Then he turned against Sven fighting him for the next 20 years supported by the inestimable booty he had taken home from his sevices in the east. His banner Landeydan <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/fairy.html> is 
2 CONC connected to Clan MacLeod <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/macleod.html>'s Fairy Flag <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/fairy.html>. Actually they are the only banners in the north that are connected to su
2 CONC perior power and magic, thus implying the idea that they were one. Harald is reported to have claimed "With this banner, I can never be defeated in battle." He named it his most important possession, even though his wealth in loot
2 CONC ed gold and precious stones is said to have been unimaginable. During his campaign against Sven of Denmark Landeydan <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/fairy.html> was to be seen in many areas of Denmark, even Haithabu 
2 CONC had been burned. In 1064 the Kings finally made peace, Harald now being 50 years of age, having fought anywhere in the world and having ruled over any part of Scandinavia.  In 1066 he started his last adventure. When Edward the Co
2 CONC nfessor <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/saxons.html> died without issue Harald Godwinson <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/saxons.html> was proclaimed King after long discussion. However William the Conqu
2 CONC eror <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/normans.html> having formerly acquired an announcment as his heir and Harald Hardradi as successor of Knut <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/saxons.html> felt, they ha
2 CONC d a stronger claim. So Harald Hardradi advised by the Earls of Orkney <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/orkney.html> and Harald Godwinsons brother Tostig the banished former Earl of Northumbria to fight against Harald 
2 CONC Godwinson <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/saxons.html>. In late Summer the english king was surprised by the norse fleet of 200 ships sailing up the Humber. Altogether with Tostig's and the orkneyinga fleet there wer
2 CONC e about 300 ships and 9000 men fighting the English. In middle september they stayed at Stamford Bridge 12 km away from York and 22 km from their ships. Harald Godwinson <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/saxons.html> s
2 CONC urprised the invaders and Hardradi tried to negotiate stating that they should not fight, if he were to keep England's North. He was answered "I GRANT YOU SEVEN FEET OF ENGLISH SOIL OR AS MUCH MORE AS YOU ARE TALLER THAN AN AVERAG
2 CONC E MAN."  Harald fell at the Battle of Stamford Bridge, an arrrow having cut his throat when leading his army. It is stated that his banner Landeydan <http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/fairy.html> had at that moment not 
2 CONC been disembarked from his ship though no one knows the reason why.
2 CONT Harald Hardruler, King of Norway, had a sign called Landeydan (Landwaster). The King's saga, Saga of Harald Sigurtharson, tells of a quarrel between Harald and Svein, a Danish king: 'Svein asked Harald what possessions of his he v
2 CONC alued most highly. He answered his banner "Land-Destroyer." Thereupon Svein asked what virtue it had to be accounted so valuable. Harald replied that it was prophesied that victory would be his before whom this banner was borne; a
2 CONC nd added that this had been the case ever since he had obtained it." Then they started to quarrel over whether this could be true.5 Harold invaded England in 1066. He was victorious under the Landeydan at York, but was defeated at
2 CONC  Stamford Bridge. There, the hardest battle was fought around the Raven banner.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Såret på Stiklestad, flyktet til Jarisleiv i Gardarike hvor han 
2 CONT ble høvding for landvernet. Reiste 1034 til Miklagard, ble 
2 CONT høvding for livvakten til keiser Mikael Katalaktes, skaffet 
2 CONT seg store rikdommer på hærferder rundt i Middelhavet.Dro 
2 CONT tilbake til Holmgard 1042 og giftet seg med Ellisiv, gikk i 
2 CONT forbund med Svein Ulvsson ( Estridsson ) som ble brutt 
2 CONT etter svik. Giftet seg med Tora Torbergsdotter Arnesson 
2 CONT 1048, forlikte seg med Svein 1064 etter flere hærferder og 
2 CONT slag. Gikk i forbund med jarl Toste Gudinesson, falt i slag 
2 CONT mot hans bror kong Harald Gudinesson ( Godwinson ) ved 
2 CONT Stamford Bridge <http://home.online.no/~olhov/slagsted.html> 1066
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
