2 CONT 870845604. Lendemann Agmund Torbergssøn GISKE died før 1050.(20790) He was married.
1 NOTE     * OCCUPATION: Lendermann
2 CONT     * BIRTH: ABT 1020, (?) (Ågmund) på Giske
2 CONT     * DEATH: 1045 
1 NOTE Øystein Orre (død 1066) var en norsk høvding av Giskeætten. Han deltok i kong Harald Hardrådes tog til England og falt i slaget ved Stamford bro.
2 CONT Øystein var sønn av Torberg Arneson på Giske og Ragnhild, datter av Erling Skjalgsson på Sola. I 1066 fulgte han sin svoger, kong Harald Hardråde, på toget til England. Da kongen ble overrumplet av Harald Godwinsson ved Stamfo
2 CONC rd bro, bevoktet Øystein flåten med en del av hæren, men ved meldingen om overfallet dro han av sted for å unnsette kongen. Han kom frem først etter kong Haralds fall, og falt selv der sammen med de fleste av sine menn.
1 NOTE Ogmund døde før sin far, dvs. tidligere enn 1050. Han var ikke lendermann.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Magnus Barefoot's Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "4. OF THORER OF STEIG.
2 CONT There was a man called Svein, a son of Harald Fietter. He was a Danish man by family, a great viking and champion, and a very clever man, and of high birth in his own country. He had been some time with King Hakon Magnuson, and wa
2 CONC s very dear to him; but after King Hakon's decease Thorer of Steig, his foster-father, had no great confidence in any treaty or friendship with King Magnus, if the whole country came into his power, on account of the position in w
2 CONC hich Thorer had stood to King Magnus, and the opposition he had made to him. Thereupon Thorer and Svein took counsel with each other, which they afterwards carried into effect, -- to raise, with Thorer's assistance, and his men, a
2 CONC  troop against Magnus. But as Thorer was old and heavy, Svein took the command, and name of leader of the troop. In this design several chiefs took part, among whom the principal was Egil Aslakson of Aurland. Egil was a lenderman,
2 CONC  and married to Ingebjorg, a daughter of Ogmund Thorbergson, a sister of Skopte of Giske. The rich and powerful man, Skjalg Erlingson, also joined their party. ..."
