1 OCCU Stallare (i.e. high official with the king's body-guard), "marshall" d'Islande, Jarl
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Úlfur Óspaksson Stallare =
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Ospak Usvivson and Aldis Ljotsdatter
2 CONT * Úlf Óspaksson ( Old Norse : Úlfr stallari Óspaksson , d . 1066) was a Viking warlord of Icelandic origin who became the right hand man and stallari ( marshal ) of Harald III of Norway . [ 1 ] [ 2 ] Quoted in Morkinskinna and Hei
2 CONC mskringla mentioned as a wise man, eloquent, great leader and honest. Grandson of Ósvífur the Wise , accompanied Norðbrikt (later Harald III) to Miklagard (Constantinople ) serving as Harald's lieutenant in the Vague guard .  He p
2 CONC articipated in multiple sieges and Viking raids in Serkland ( land of the Saracens ) and shared prison when King Harald was imprisoned by Miguel V . He participated in the Battle of Niså , with his ship always flanking his king, w
2 CONC hen Harald returned to Norway to claim the throne. For his special affection and service, King Harald gave him half a fief and the rights as lendmann, plus twelve silver marks as compensation.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT *Married: '''Jorunn Thorbergsdotter''' (b. 1027), daughter of Torberg Arnesson . As a result of that relationship would be born a son, Jon den Staerke Ulfsson (nicknamed the Strong , n. 1055), father Erland himald Jonsson (b. 1087
2 CONC ) who was the father of the archbishop of Trondheim , Eystein Erlandsson (1119 - 1188).  JORUNN Thorbergsdotter .  Morkinskinna records the marriage of “Jórunn, the daughter of Thorbergr Árnason” and “Úlfr Óspaksson…the marshal.  
2 CONC Snorre names "Jorun, Thorberg's daughter, a sister of Harald's wife Thora" as wife of "Ulf Uspakson…his marshal" and their children "Joan the Strong of Rasvol, and Brigida mother of Sauda-Ulf, who was father of Peter Byrdar-Svein,
2 CONC  father of Ulf Fly and Sigrid.  Joan the Strong's son was Erlend Himalde, father of Archbishop Eystein and his brothers".  married '''ULF Ospaksson Stallare''' (-1066).  Descendants in ES II 107.  - https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLand
2 CONC s/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#ThoraThorbergsdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Jón strong in Rásvöllur,''' Jon's strong son was Erlendur Hidaldi, father of Archbishop Eystein and his brothers.
2 CONT * '''Brigid Ulfsdatter,''' the mother of Sauda-Ulf, the father of Peter Burdensvein, their father Ulf Flise.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Heimskringla / Harald Saga of Sigurðarson / 37=
2 CONT
2 CONT Wolf Óspaksson was in great love with King Harald. He was the wisest man, clever in speech, great overlord, confident and simple. King Harald made Wolf his stallion and married him to Jórunni Thorbergsdóttir, sister of Thora, whom
2 CONC  King Harald had. The children of Ulf and Jórunn were Jón strong in Rásvöllur and Brigid, the mother of Sauda-Ulf, the father of Peter Burdensvein, their father Ulf Flise. Jon's strong son was Erlendur Hidaldi, father of Archbisho
2 CONC p Eystein and his brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Harald gave the landlord's Wolf the right and twelve mark parties and over half a county in Trondheim. So says Steinn Herdísarson in the Wolf Party.
2 CONT
