2 CONT Last Edited=7 Mar 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Jatoslawa of Novgorod is the daughter of Jarislaus I, Grand Duke of Kiev and Ingegarde of Sweden. (2), (3) She married Harald III Hardrade, King of Norway, son of Sigurd Syr, King of Ringeringe and Asta (?), in 1045. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jatoslawa of Novgorod was also known as Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jatoslawa of Novgorod and Harald III Hardrade, King of Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Maria (?) d. 1066
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Ingegard (?)+ (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. Magnus II Haraldsson, King of Norway+ b. 1049, d. 1069 (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT -4. Olav III Haraldsson, King of Norway+ b. 1050, d. c 1093 (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 16. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.[S16] Louda and MacLagan, Lines of Succession, table 24.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.[S262] Russia, online http://www.friesian.com/russia.htm. Hereinafter cited as Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Russia Rurikid:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT IELIZAVETA Iaroslavna (-after 25 Sep 1066).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorre records the marriage of King Harald and Elisabeth "called by the Northmen Ellisif" daughter of "King Jarisleif", specifying in a later passage that "the Swedish king Olaf…was brother of [her] mother"[167].  Morkinskinna rec
2 CONC ords the marriage of “Haraldr Sigurdarson” and “King Yaroslav and Queen Ingigerdr…daughter…Elisabeth, the Norsemen call her Ellisif”[168].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorre records that "Queen Ellisif came from the West…with her stepson Olaf and her daughter Ingegerd" after her husband was killed[169].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (1044) HARALD Sigurdson, son of SIGURD Syr King of Ringeringe & his wife Asta Gudbrandsdatter (1015-killed in battle Stamfordbridge 25 Sep 1066).  He succeeded in 1047 as HARALD III "Hardråde" King of Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the English Wikipedia page of Elisiv of Kiev:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elisiv_of_Kiev
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisaveta Yaroslavna of Kiev (in Norwegian: Ellisif or Elisabeth), (1025 - ca 1067), was a Rus' Princess of Kiev and a Norwegian queen, wife and queen consort of king Harald III of Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisaveta was born to Prince Yaroslav I of Kiev and Princess Ingegerd Olofsdotter of Sweden. She was the sister of Anne of Kiev, queen and regent of France, and Anastasia of Kiev, queen of Hungary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the winter of 1043-44, Elisaveta was married to Prince Harald Sigurdsson of Norway, who was in service of her father at the time. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1045, she followed Harald to Norway, were they became king and queen of Norway. In Norway, she was called Queen Elisiv. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1047, her husband became the sole ruler. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1048, Harald took another wife, Tora Torbergsdatter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1066, Harald invaded England, where he died. Elisiv and her daughters followed Harald to England, where Maria died, as it was said, at the news of her father's death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisiv and her second daughter Ingegerd returned to Norway with the Norwegian fleet. She lived the rest of her life with her step-son King Olav Kyrre on Ostlandet. She is not likely to have lived long as a widow, and is presumed t
2 CONC o have died the year after she was widowed, although the year of her death is unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It has sometime been said, that she married King Sweyn II of Denmark as a widow, but she may have been confused with Harald's second wife Tora Torbergsdatter, who is also suggested to have married Sweyn as a widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisaveta was married to Harald in 1043 or 1044. They had two known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Maria Haraldsdotter of Norway, died in England 1066.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Ingegerd of Norway, (d. 1120), queen of Denmark and Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT This article is a translation of its equivalent on Bulgarian Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorre Sturlason: Snorres kongesagaer, bind II: «Harald Hårfagres saga» side 217. Oslo 2003.
2 CONT
