1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ingegerd of Norway=
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingegerd Haraldsdotter of Norway (Old Norse: Ingigerðr Haraldsdóttir, c. 1046 – c. 1120) was a medieval Scandinavian Queen, Princess of Norway, and the Queen consort first of [https://www.geni.com/people/Oluf-I-Hunger-King-of-Denm
2 CONC ark/347868854190012671 King Olaf I of Denmark] (died 1095) and second of [https://www.geni.com/people/Philip-Halstensson-King-of-Sweden/4274386 King Philip of Sweden] (died 1118).
2 CONT
2 CONT Continue on Wikipedia: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingegerd_of_Norway English], [https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingegjerd_Haraldsdatter Norsk bokmål], [https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingegerd_Haraldsdatter Dansk], [https://sv.wik
2 CONC ipedia.org/wiki/Ingegerd_Haraldsdotter Svenska]
2 CONT
2 CONT The years of her birth and death are not confirmed, but she is known to have survived her second spouse.
