1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jon Svaleson Smør (c. 1420–1483) was a Norwegian knight, riksråd and regent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon was a son of the knight Svale Jonson Smør and his wife Sigrid Gunnarsdotter Kane. He was a knight from 1449, and cabinet minister from 1458. In the 1470s he was a fehird (tax minister) and høvedsmann (lord) of the king's farm.
2 CONC  Later, he was one of main forces behind the reactivation of the Norwegian Riksråd at the end of the reign of King Christian I. As a riksråd, and from 1482 regent, he led the policy of the Riksråd to maintain Norway's political in
2 CONC terests during the interregnum between 1481 and 1483.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon was probably after 1450 married to Gudrun Olavsdatter (c. 1415–1476/86), daughter of the knight Olav Håkonsson and Ingebjørg Jonsdotter. It is unknown if they ever had any children together. Jon died of drowning at Jersøy, nea
2 CONC r Tønsberg, the last man in the direct male line of the Smør family.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Svaleson_Smør
2 CONT
2 CONT https://nbl.snl.no/Jon_Svalesson_Smør
