2 CONT ==[http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Soga_um_Inge  Heimskringla Soga (kap 17)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 17. Kyrpinga-Orm and Ragnhild, his daughter Sveinke Steinarsson, had a son named Erling. His father's KyrpingaOrm was named Svein, and he was the son of Svein Erlendsson from Gjerde [59]. His mother Orm was Ragna, who was the daug
2 CONC hter of Earl Orm Eilivsson [60] and Sigrid [61], who was the daughter of Earl Finn Arneson. Earl Orm Eilivsson's mother was Ragnhild, daughter of Earl Haakon the mighty. Erling was a wise man and a good friend of King Inge, and wi
2 CONC th his consent Erling Kristin, daughter of King Sigurd Jorsalafar and Queen Malmfrid. Erling had a farm on Studla [62] on Sunnhordaland. Erling went [1150] out of the country, and with him accompanied Eindride Unge and even more l
2 CONC ieutenants, and had a beautiful here. They set out on a Jorsala voyage and went west across the sea to the Orkney Islands. From there Earl Rognvald was with them, whom they called Kale, and Bishop Vilhjalm, and they had a total of
2 CONC  15 longships, when they sailed from the Orkney Islands, and so they sailed to the Sudrøyans and from there [1151] west to Valland and then the same road as King Sigurd Jorsalafar had gone out to Norvasund, and ravaged far and wid
2 CONC e in the heathen Spain. Immediately after they had sailed through sound, Eindride Unge parted, and those who followed him, with 6 ships from them, and then they left for themselves. Earl Rognvald and Erling Skakke fell into the se
2 CONC a on a dromund [63] and docked with 9 ships and fought with him. At last the carpenters laid their ranks under the dromund, and then the heathens threw down on them both weapons and stones and pots full of boiling dog and oil. Erl
2 CONC ing lay closest to them with his ship, so weapons to the heathens came outside his ship. Then Erling and his men cut holes in the dromund, some in the waterway and some up on the ship's deck, so they slipped in there. This is what
2 CONC  Torbjørn Skakke-skald told in Erlingsdraapa. The man who first went up on the dromund, was called Audun Raude and was his ancestor Erling. They took the dream and killed a lot of people and got a lot of booty and won a glorious s
2 CONC aying. On this voyage Earl Rognvald and Erling Skakke came to Jorsalaland and out to Jordan-aai. There they turned and went first to Miklegard, and there they left the ship and went home by land, and everything went well [1153], u
2 CONC ntil they came to Norway, and they went big word of this journey. Erling now went on to be a much greater man than before, both by this skill and by his marriage goal; he was attaat a wise man, rich and great-granddaughter and wor
2 CONC d-hitter, and he kept himself in all things most friends with King Inge of the three brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Stødle family, Norwegian nobility from the Middle Ages, named after the farm Stødle (now Støle) in Etne, Sunnhordland. The family descended from Erlend av Gerde (Gjerde in Etne), who was one of the farmers' leaders in the batt
2 CONC le of Stiklestad 1030. Erlend's grandson's son was the employed lieutenant Orm Sveinsson (Kyrpinga-Orm). Orm's son Erling (Skakke) married Sigurd Jorsalfare's daughter Kristine, and was the father of King Magnus Erlingsson. Both K
2 CONC yrpinga-Orm and Erling Skakke lived in Stødle.
2 CONT
