2 CONT >>>>m [http://www.geni.com/people/H%C3%A1vard/6000000006906186717?through=6000000003097958665 HAVARD] (-winter 988/89).  Steward of Caithness for Jarl Sigurd.  Killed by Jarls Melsnati and Hundi, who were defeated when Jarl Sigurd
2 CONC  attacked them in revenge.][http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>g)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Skuli-Thorfinnsson/6000000003097952792  SKULI] Torfinnsson (-killed in battle).  Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Arnfinn…Havard the Fecund…Hlodvir…Ljot…Skuli” as the five sons of Thorfin
2 CONC n[851].  Snorre names "the Earls Hlodver, Arnfid, Ljot and Skule, the sons of Thorfin Hausakljufer" as rulers in Orkney when Queen Gunhild and her sons returned to Orkney[852].  In a later saga, Snorre names (in order) "Arnfin, Ha
2 CONC vard, Hlodver, Liot and Skule" as sons of Thorfin "Hausakljufer"[853].  Orkneyinga Saga records that “Skuli, Ljot´s brother” was given “the title earl by the King of Scots”, before going north to Caithness from where he sailed to 
2 CONC Orkney to claim the islands, but was defeated and fled “first over to Caithness and then south to Scotland” and later killed[854].  The uncertain chronology of events recorded in Orkneyinga Saga make it difficult to be certain abo
2 CONC ut the identity of the Scottish king in question, although Kenneth II (who ruled from 971 to 995) appears the most likely possibility.  It is interesting to note that the text does not specify that Skuli was made “Earl of Caithnes
2 CONC s” just earl without a territorial epithet, reminiscent of the position in many other European countries at the time where the title was not linked to the landholding.]  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_To
2 CONC c268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
