2 CONT Cellach mac Cerbaill (nicknamed Cellach of the Hard Conflicts) was king of Osraige from 905 to his death in 908
2 CONT
2 CONT Ceallach was a son of king Cerball of Osraige. He took part in the battle of Gowran in 893.[3] He came to the throne after the deposition of his older brother Diarmait in 905. Along with his son Muircheartach, he was slain in the 
2 CONC battle of Mag Ailbe fighting on the side of the illustrious king-bishop of Cashel Cormac mac Cuilennáin in 908. The Annals of Inisfallen record his death in 908:
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cellach_mac_Cerbaill]
