1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Gudbrand Olavsson «Kula»=
2 CONT
2 CONT Also known as Gudbrandi Culu
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Olav Einarsson Breid and Gudbjørg (Jari) Ufeigsdotter Breid 
2 CONT * Born ca. 923 ) from Opplandene. 
2 CONT * He is remembered as he was the father of Åsta Gudbrandsdatter from Vestfold (born 970 ), and thus the grandfather of the later kings Olav the Holy and Harald Hardråde
2 CONT * Gudbrand is mentioned in Snorre Sturlason's saga about Olav Tryggvasson and in the legendary saga of Olav the Holy.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Ulfhilde  (Gunhild) Thorasdottir,''' daughter of Hallur and Thora Audunarsdottir Mosháls. Gunhild Thorasdottir was born circa 927 in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Åsta Gudbrandsdatter''' daughter of Gudbrand Olavsson «Kula» married Vestfold king Harald Grenske  . According to Snorre Sturlasson , Harald went to Sweden and marched to Sigrid Storråde because she was of a better lineage th
2 CONC an his wife. Sigrid rejected the courtship and killed him by bestowing him full and burning him inside. Gudbrand lived in the present Hole municipality, which Åsta moved back to when Harald Grenske was killed in 995 , the same yea
2 CONC r that Olav the Saints was born. Gudbrand participated in the upbringing of his daughter Olav until Åsta married Sigurd Syr (Halvdansson) [3] . Åsta later gave birth to half-brother to Olav, later King Harald Hardråd Sigurdsson . 
2 CONC She also had sons Guttorm Sigurdsson and Halvdan Sigurdsson, and daughter Ingerid Sigurdsdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://no.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gudbrand_Kula Gudbrand Kula, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudbrand Kula (Gudbrand Olavsson Kula) (born ca. 923 , died 970 ) from the Uplands. He is remembered because he was the father of Åsta Gudbrandsdatter from Vestfold (born 970 ), and thus the grandfather of the later kings Olav the
2 CONC  Holy and Harald Hardråde . He was married to Ulvhild.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudbrand is mentioned in Snorri Sturlason's saga of Olav Tryggvasson and in The legendary saga of Olav the saint , chapter 1. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Åsta Gudbrandsdatter was married to Vestfold king Harald Grenske [2] . According to Snorre Sturlasson, Harald went to Sweden and proposed to Sigrid Storråde because she was of better blood than the wife he had. Sigrid rejected the
2 CONC  proposal and killed him by getting him drunk and burning him inside.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudbrand lived in the current municipality of Hole , which Åsta moved back to when Harald Grenske was killed in 995 , the same year that Olav the saint was born. Gudbrand participated in the upbringing of his daughter Olav until Å
2 CONC sta married Sigurd Syr (Halvdansson) [3] . Åsta later gave birth to Olav's half-brother, the later King Harald Hardråde Sigurdsson . She also had sons Guttorm Sigurdsson and Halvdan Sigurdsson, and daughter Ingerid Sigurdsdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
