2 CONC n to King Æthelwulf of the Anglo-Saxons who was hastening on his way to Rome. Charles gave him all the supplies a king might need and had him escorted right to the boundary of his realm with all the courtesies due to a king.”  The
2 CONC  biography of Pope Benedict III in the ‘Liber Pontificalis’ (Book of the Popes) notes that Æthelwulf arrived at Rome “with a multitude of people”, and lists the valuable gifts he donated to St Peter, including “a fine gold crown w
2 CONC eighing 4 pounds” and “sword bound with fine gold”.  According to William of Malmesbury (‘GR’ II §109), Æthelwulf: “nobly repaired the English School [in Rome], which, according to report, was first founded by Offa, king of the Me
