2 CONC  and gifts, Æthelwulf sailed with Judith to Britain where his kingdom lay.”  Judith was twelve or thirteen years-old at this time. The mother of Alfred, and as far as is known all of Æthelwulf's children, was called Osburh: “an ex
2 CONC tremely devout woman, noble in mind, noble also by descent; she was daughter to Oslac, the famous cupbearer of King Æthelwulf”, says Asser (§2). Presumably Osburh had died by, or during, the time of Æthelwulf's sojourn in Rome. ..
